      <article class="doc-texto">
      <h2 id="section-1">1. Who we are and acceptance of these terms</h2>
      <p>Rosetta Quantum is a brand of <strong>Blue Tuna SpA</strong>, a company incorporated in Chile. In these terms, "we", "us" and "Rosetta Quantum" mean Blue Tuna SpA.</p>
      <p>By using rosettaquantum.com or our public API, or by ordering any of our services, you accept these terms. If you do not agree with them, please do not use the site or the services.</p>
      <h2 id="section-2">2. What we offer</h2>
      <ul><li><strong>Measurement experiments on quantum hardware.</strong> Paid services (such as Exploration, Full experiment and the Measurement Program) in which we design, run and measure an experiment and deliver a report with sealed, verifiable results. The current catalog and prices are published at <a href="https://rosettaquantum.com/pricing/">rosettaquantum.com/pricing/</a>.</li><li><strong>Sealed public evidence.</strong> Experiment results are cryptographically sealed (SHA-256 hashes, with OpenTimestamps anchoring on Bitcoin) and published in a public evidence archive that anyone can verify.</li><li><strong>Monitor.</strong> A monthly subscription, described in section 9.</li><li><strong>Other products</strong> (such as the Q-Ready Kit), as described at /pricing/.</li><li><strong>Free services.</strong> Access to the evidence archive, the public API and the Q-Ready Map are free of charge, subject to the acceptable-use rules in section 5.</li></ul>
      <h2 id="section-3">3. Ordering, payment and refunds</h2>
      <p>Payments are handled by <strong>Paddle.com</strong>, acting as <strong>Merchant of Record</strong>: Paddle is the seller of record for your purchase and handles checkout, invoicing, applicable taxes/VAT, and processes refunds to your original payment method. Paddle's buyer terms apply to the purchase itself.</p>
      <p>Our refund policy follows the principle published on our pricing page: <em>"refund on the result: you pay for the measurement, not for the verdict."</em> In practice:</p>
      <ul><li>You may request a <strong>full refund, no questions asked, within 14 days of delivery of the deliverable</strong>.</li><li>A <strong>negative result is a delivered result</strong>. It is a valid deliverable and is charged exactly like a positive one. The 14-day no-questions refund window applies regardless of whether the result was the one you hoped for.</li><li>For the Monitor subscription, see section 9.</li></ul>
      <p>To request a refund, write to <strong><a href="mailto:hello@rosettaquantum.com">hello@rosettaquantum.com</a></strong>.</p>
      <h2 id="section-4">4. Deliverables and the public evidence model</h2>
      <ul><li>Every paid experiment includes a <strong>report</strong>, delivered to you.</li><li>The experiment's <strong>seals</strong> (SHA-256 hashes and their OpenTimestamps anchoring) are <strong>published in the public evidence archive by design</strong> and can be verified by anyone.</li><li>Your <strong>underlying data can remain private</strong>: only its hash is published. What becomes public is the proof that the data existed in a given form at a given time — not the data itself — unless you choose to publish the data.</li></ul>
      <h2 id="section-5">5. Acceptable use of the site and public API</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul><li>misrepresent seals or evidence — for example, presenting a seal as covering data it does not cover, or presenting unsealed material as sealed;</li><li>disrupt the service, including scraping or automated requests at a volume that degrades it for others;</li><li>impersonate Rosetta Quantum or claim that we endorse conclusions we have not sealed;</li><li>use the site or the API for unlawful purposes.</li></ul>
      <p>We may throttle or block access that breaks these rules.</p>
      <h2 id="section-6">6. Intellectual property</h2>
      <ul><li><strong>Your report is yours to use and share</strong>, publicly or privately.</li><li><strong>The public evidence archive is public by design</strong> and may be consulted and verified by anyone.</li><li><strong>Our site content, code and methods remain the property of Blue Tuna SpA.</strong> These terms do not transfer them.</li></ul>
      <h2 id="section-7">7. Disclaimers</h2>
      <ul><li>What we sell is a <strong>sealed, verifiable measurement</strong>. A measurement is not a guarantee: <strong>results can be negative</strong>, and a negative result is a valid deliverable.</li><li>We make <strong>no claims of quantum advantage or supremacy</strong>, and we do not promise any specific result, performance improvement or business outcome.</li><li>Nothing on this site, in the evidence archive or in our deliverables is <strong>investment, financial, legal or medical advice</strong>.</li></ul>
      <h2 id="section-8">8. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, our total liability for any claim related to a service is <strong>limited to the fees you paid for that service</strong>. We are not liable for indirect or consequential damages. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited under applicable law.</p>
      <h2 id="section-9">9. Monitor subscription</h2>
      <ul><li>Monitor is a <strong>monthly subscription</strong> at the price published at /pricing/.</li><li>You may <strong>cancel at any time</strong>. Cancellation takes effect at the <strong>end of the current billing period</strong>; you will not be charged again after that.</li><li>The <strong>first charge is refundable within 14 days</strong>.</li><li>Billing and refunds are processed by Paddle (section 3).</li></ul>
      <h2 id="section-10">10. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>We may update these terms. The current version is always published on this page, with its publication date shown at the top. If you keep using the site or the services after a change is published, that means you accept the updated terms.</p>
      <h2 id="section-11">11. Governing law and contact</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of <strong>Chile</strong>.</p>
      <p>Questions about these terms: <strong><a href="mailto:hello@rosettaquantum.com">hello@rosettaquantum.com</a></strong>.</p>
      <h2 id="refunds" class="doc-parte">Refund Policy</h2>
      <p><strong>Rosetta Quantum</strong> is a brand of <strong>Blue Tuna SpA</strong> (Chile). Payments are handled by <strong>Paddle.com</strong>, which acts as Merchant of Record: Paddle is the seller of record for your purchase, runs the checkout, issues the invoice, handles taxes/VAT, and processes refunds. Paddle's buyer terms apply to the purchase itself.</p>
      <h3 id="refunds-1">1. The principle: you pay for the measurement, not for the verdict</h3>
      <p>What we sell is a sealed, verifiable <strong>measurement</strong>, not a favorable outcome. We never promise specific results, performance, or business outcomes — and results can be negative.</p>
      <p>A <strong>negative result is a complete, valid deliverable</strong>. It is measured, sealed, and reported with the same care as a positive one, and it is charged the same way. A negative result does not by itself void or discount your invoice.</p>
      <p>The refund right described below applies to every paid product <strong>regardless of whether your result was positive or negative</strong> — that is the point: the refund is about your purchase, not about the verdict.</p>
      <p>Our deliverables are measurements, not advice. Nothing we deliver constitutes medical, financial, or investment advice.</p>
      <h3 id="refunds-2">2. Full refund, no questions asked</h3>
      <p>For every <strong>one-off paid product</strong>, you can request a <strong>full refund, no questions asked, within 14 days of delivery of your deliverable</strong>. For the <strong>Monitor</strong> subscription, see section 3.</p>
      <ul><li>You do not need to give a reason.</li><li>The refund is for the full amount you paid.</li><li>Products listed as free at <a href="https://rosettaquantum.com/pricing/">rosettaquantum.com/pricing/</a> involve no payment, so there is nothing to refund.</li></ul>
      <p>Current products and prices are published at <a href="https://rosettaquantum.com/pricing/">rosettaquantum.com/pricing/</a>.</p>
      <h3 id="refunds-3">3. Monitor subscription</h3>
      <p><strong>Monitor</strong> is a monthly subscription.</p>
      <ul><li>You can <strong>cancel anytime</strong>. Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period; you keep access until then.</li><li><strong>Only your first charge is refundable</strong> — in full, within 14 days of that charge, no questions asked. Later charges are not refundable under this policy; instead, you can cancel at any time.</li><li>If you have questions or need help with cancellation, contact us at <strong><a href="mailto:hello@rosettaquantum.com">hello@rosettaquantum.com</a></strong> with the order reference from your Paddle receipt.</li></ul>
      <h3 id="refunds-4">4. How to request a refund</h3>
      <ol><li>Email <strong><a href="mailto:hello@rosettaquantum.com">hello@rosettaquantum.com</a></strong> with the <strong>order reference from your Paddle receipt</strong>.</li><li>That's it — no justification needed.</li></ol>
      <p>Refunds are processed by <strong>Paddle</strong> to the <strong>original payment method</strong> used for the purchase.</p>
      <h3 id="refunds-5">5. Your statutory rights</h3>
      <p>This policy adds to — and does not limit or replace — any rights you have as a consumer under applicable law. Our relationship with you is governed by the law of <strong>Chile</strong>. Paddle's buyer terms apply to the purchase transaction itself.</p>
